(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-proc/src/sh.asl#" :text "AgentScript Shell & Process Automation Engine: Subprocess execution, pipelines & logging (d-446d). A receipt's spoolPath is a real file holding the command's exact raw bytes; it persists until releaseReceipt! is called.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-proc/src/sh.asl#boundPortHeadWindow" :text "Bounds detectBoundPort's input to its first 64KB (PROC-spoolQuadratic round 2d, fixing round 2c): a server's startup banner prints near the start of its output, not the end, so a last-64KB tail could miss an early banner behind more than 64KB of later output, or find a later, different match and report the wrong port. Scanning the head instead preserves detectBoundPort's first-match semantics exactly whenever that match falls in the first 64KB, while still capping stringLower's cost at a constant.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-proc/src/spool.asl#" :text "APM Two-Tier Spooling: bounded 200-line RAM ring buffer and 10MB circular ephemeral disk spool. The disk tier persists at its spoolPath until a caller explicitly releases it (spoolUnlink!/spoolPathRelease!); nothing here deletes it automatically.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-proc/src/spool.asl#RingBuffer.capacity" :text "Maximum number of lines retained in resident RAM (default 200)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-proc/src/spool.asl#RingBuffer.lines" :text "Retained stream lines in FIFO order")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-proc/src/spool.asl#RingBuffer.count" :text "Total line count currently held in buffer")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-proc/src/spool.asl#DiskSpool.path" :text "Filesystem path to ephemeral disk spool")
